   "text": {
    "L1": "Some objects give out their own light. We call them luminous.",
    "L2": "The Sun, a candle flame, a glowing bulb and a firefly are luminous sources.",
    "L3": "The Moon is not luminous. It shines because sunlight reflects from it into our eyes.",
    "L4": "Objects that do not make their own light are non-luminous. We see them when light is reflected into our eyes.",
    "L5": "Transparent materials let almost all light pass, so we see clearly through them.",
    "L6": "Translucent materials let some light pass, but not clearly. Opaque materials let no light pass.",
    "L7": "Now classify this material: which one is translucent?"
   },
